%% Novara — authentication flow (Clerk)
%% See docs/Engineering-Bible/08-Authentication.md
sequenceDiagram
    participant U as User
    participant FE as project-novara (App.tsx)
    participant CProxy as clerkProxyMiddleware<br/>(/api/__clerk)
    participant Clerk as Clerk Frontend/Backend API
    participant BE as api-server routes

    U->>FE: visits /sign-in
    FE->>FE: renders Clerk <SignIn><br/>(forceRedirectUrl=/dashboard)
    FE->>CProxy: Clerk Frontend API calls<br/>proxied via VITE_CLERK_PROXY_URL
    CProxy->>CProxy: getClerkProxyHost(req)<br/>resolves canonical hostname
    CProxy->>Clerk: forwarded request<br/>(Clerk-Secret-Key, Clerk-Proxy-Url headers)
    Clerk-->>CProxy: auth challenge / session result
    CProxy-->>FE: proxied response
    U->>FE: submits credentials
    Clerk-->>FE: session established, JWT issued
    FE->>FE: routerPush("/dashboard")<br/>(wouter setLocation)

    Note over FE,BE: Every subsequent API call:
    FE->>BE: fetch with Authorization: Bearer <JWT>
    BE->>BE: clerkMiddleware verifies JWT<br/>(publishableKeyFromHost resolves instance)
    BE->>BE: requireAuth reads getAuth(req).userId
    alt invalid/missing session
        BE-->>FE: 401 Unauthorized
    else valid session
        BE->>BE: req.userId = verified Clerk userId<br/>(never trusts client-supplied userId)
        BE-->>FE: 200 + data scoped to req.userId
    end

    Note over FE: ClerkQueryClientCacheInvalidator<br/>clears TanStack Query cache<br/>whenever the signed-in userId changes
